  "contract": [
    "Null frame-table owner returns0 before modifying state. Otherwise OR the complete request into started before checking memory status exactly1; any other byte returns-1.",
    "Loop20 slots. Native ordered reads are live frame owner, initialized byte, frame pointer, even when the initialized byte is1. Only exactly1 skips initialization. A null callback still runs the disabled strategy hook.",
    "Callback return low byte is retained, success alone stores init flag1, and error exits after the strategy hook. Strategy is stock BX LR and has no observable state.",
    "ADT clears byte2,0,1 in that order. HR uses current16-bit rate, maps engine full-word zero to success, then clears result byte0 and reloaded result word4 even on failure.",
    "HRV success writes127 at algorithm+2. It then reloads the global frame table and clears the HR slot result byte, and resets the shared initialization word even on failure. The counter-like symbol name does not establish a broader counter meaning.",
    "SpO2 maps full-word engine zero to success. Soft ADT null frame is accepted; otherwise clear flag0, set flag1 iff function word equals0x8000, invoke the engine, and ignore its return."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Tests execute actual C controller, adapters, status and strategy; four deeper engine initializers are modeled and remain unresolved imports. Added four named engine boundaries replace the one unresolved high-level controller, so application import count rises60 to63. This does not establish complete sensor initialization.",
    "All256 memory-status bytes,64 callback masks,20 individual request bits, full/high-bit masks, initialized bytes0/1/2/255, engine full-word results, fail positions, sample-rate/type boundaries, null accepted paths and live provider mutation cases compared.",
    "All282 native instruction bytes execute. Exact public read order/width and write order/width/value, engine arguments/state snapshots, final state, saved integer/FP registers, SP, masks and guards compare. Source cannot execute stock; modeled ports return through BX LR instructions.",
    "Started-bitmap and null/unready/already-initialized returns have independent oracles. Invalid frame pointers, low-address faults, cold FP activation, interrupt concurrency and physical hardware behavior are unproven. Caller scratch, APSR and private frames excluded.",
    "Memory struct moves into shared header without changing the config machine object. Frame owner, started bitmap,20 init bytes, memory-ready byte and ADT flags reuse existing owners. New ownership is4-byte initialization word at20007c2c and2 flags at20007c30; full physical RAM/startup placement remains open.",
    "All867 other prior nongenerated source/object pairs unchanged; tested object equals the normal879-unit build. Existing generated startup/uecc differ. Source-plan and cache composition layout unchanged.",
    "No instruction or image identity claimed. Final executable linking/startup, remaining engine/hardware dependencies and device boot remain open; ld-r composition is not bootable firmware."
  ],
